{"title":"About","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"About","about":{"template":"trestles","image":"assets/anthony-raborn.jpg","image-shape":"rounded","links":[{"icon":"bluesky","text":"Bluesky","href":"https://bsky.app/profile/raborndecisionsciences.com"},{"icon":"github","text":"Github","href":"https://github.com/raborn-decision-sciences"},{"icon":"linkedin","text":"LinkedIn","href":"https://www.linkedin.com/company/raborn-decision-sciences"},{"icon":"envelope-fill","text":"Email","href":"mailto:hello@raborndecisionsciences.com"}]},"toc":false},"headingText":"Education","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\nI'm Anthony Raborn, a psychometrician and statistician. I specialize in applied measurement, reproducible analytics, and custom R/Shiny decision tools.\n\nMy work combines psychometric methods, statistical programming, and practical software development to help organizations make clearer decisions from complex assessment and operational data. I try to build tools that are easy to repeat, explain, and use at any level of technical expertise.\n\nI've been consulting off and on since graduate school, and I now do that work as Raborn Decision Sciences.\n\n\nPhD in Research and Evaluation Methodology, Minor in Statistics\n\nUniversity of Florida | Gainesville, FL | May 2019\n\n## Areas of expertise\n\n- Psychometrics and assessment analytics\n- Item analysis, DIF, equating, standard setting, and technical reporting\n- R package development, deployment, and reproducible workflows\n- Shiny dashboards and decision-support tools\n- Quarto reports and technical documentation\n- Operations and break-even modeling\n\n## Selected publications\n\nThe first four describe the methods used in my R packages. The last is from my applied work on clinical trials. The full list is on [ORCID](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8083-4739).\n\n::: {.rds-cites}\nRaborn & Leite (2018). [ShortForm: An R package to select scale short forms with the ant colony optimization algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1177/0146621617752993). *Applied Psychological Measurement*.\n\nRaborn, Leite & Marcoulides (2020). [A comparison of metaheuristic optimization algorithms for scale short-form development](https://doi.org/10.1177/0013164420906600). *Educational and Psychological Measurement*.\n\nRaborn & Sarı (2021). [Mixed adaptive multistage testing: A new approach](https://doi.org/10.21031/epod.871014). *Journal of Measurement and Evaluation in Education and Psychology*.\n\nHuggins-Manley, Raborn, et al. (2024). [A nonparametric composite group DIF index for focal groups stemming from multicategorical variables](https://doi.org/10.1111/jedm.12394). *Journal of Educational Measurement*.\n\nRaborn et al. (2025). [Psychometric analysis of the Neuro-QoL Fatigue in generalized myasthenia gravis using data from a phase 3 trial](https://doi.org/10.1007/s11136-025-03998-9). *Quality of Life Research*.\n:::\n\n## Technical toolkit\n\n[Programming and reporting]{.rds-kicker}\nR, Shiny, Quarto, SQL, Git/GitHub, Python\n\n[Psychometric and statistical software]{.rds-kicker}\nWinsteps, flexMIRT, Mplus\n\n## Resume/CV\n\n[Interactive CV](cv/index.html){.btn .btn-outline-secondary target=\"_self\"} [Download consulting CV](assets/raborn-decision-sciences-cv.docx){.btn .btn-outline-secondary}\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\nI'm Anthony Raborn, a psychometrician and statistician. I specialize in applied measurement, reproducible analytics, and custom R/Shiny decision tools.\n\nMy work combines psychometric methods, statistical programming, and practical software development to help organizations make clearer decisions from complex assessment and operational data. I try to build tools that are easy to repeat, explain, and use at any level of technical expertise.\n\nI've been consulting off and on since graduate school, and I now do that work as Raborn Decision Sciences.\n\n## Education\n\nPhD in Research and Evaluation Methodology, Minor in Statistics\n\nUniversity of Florida | Gainesville, FL | May 2019\n\n## Areas of expertise\n\n- Psychometrics and assessment analytics\n- Item analysis, DIF, equating, standard setting, and technical reporting\n- R package development, deployment, and reproducible workflows\n- Shiny dashboards and decision-support tools\n- Quarto reports and technical documentation\n- Operations and break-even modeling\n\n## Selected publications\n\nThe first four describe the methods used in my R packages. The last is from my applied work on clinical trials. The full list is on [ORCID](https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8083-4739).\n\n::: {.rds-cites}\nRaborn & Leite (2018). [ShortForm: An R package to select scale short forms with the ant colony optimization algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1177/0146621617752993). *Applied Psychological Measurement*.\n\nRaborn, Leite & Marcoulides (2020). [A comparison of metaheuristic optimization algorithms for scale short-form development](https://doi.org/10.1177/0013164420906600). *Educational and Psychological Measurement*.\n\nRaborn & Sarı (2021). [Mixed adaptive multistage testing: A new approach](https://doi.org/10.21031/epod.871014). *Journal of Measurement and Evaluation in Education and Psychology*.\n\nHuggins-Manley, Raborn, et al. (2024). [A nonparametric composite group DIF index for focal groups stemming from multicategorical variables](https://doi.org/10.1111/jedm.12394). *Journal of Educational Measurement*.\n\nRaborn et al. (2025). [Psychometric analysis of the Neuro-QoL Fatigue in generalized myasthenia gravis using data from a phase 3 trial](https://doi.org/10.1007/s11136-025-03998-9). *Quality of Life Research*.\n:::\n\n## Technical toolkit\n\n[Programming and reporting]{.rds-kicker}\nR, Shiny, Quarto, SQL, Git/GitHub, Python\n\n[Psychometric and statistical software]{.rds-kicker}\nWinsteps, flexMIRT, Mplus\n\n## Resume/CV\n\n[Interactive CV](cv/index.html){.btn .btn-outline-secondary target=\"_self\"} [Download consulting CV](assets/raborn-decision-sciences-cv.docx){.btn .btn-outline-secondary}\n"}